WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:08.050
More than 2,500 left-handed people are killed
each year whilst using equipment designed

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:12.440
for right-handed people, the most dangerous
of which is the right-handed power saw.

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:15.099
Life sure can be hard for a lefty.

00:00:15.099 --> 00:00:19.960
The word right is synonymous with the word
“correct” whereas “left” comes from

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:23.600
Old English where it meant “sinister”
and “evil”.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:28.270
In old England Left-handedness was actually
believed to have come from the devil.

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:34.410
So if left-handedness is such a disadvantage
then why are between 10% and 12% of the population

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:36.730
still left handed?

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:40.400
After all, evolution typically weeds out imperfections
within a species.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:46.850
But scientists have found evidence that as
far back as 500,000 years ago, 10% of humans

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:50.329
were left-handed; it’s always been this
way.

00:00:50.329 --> 00:00:55.260
So there must still be some advantage to being
left-handed, even in the modern world.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:56.739
So what is it?

00:00:56.739 --> 00:01:02.450
Left’s find out.

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:05.780
Contrary to some theories left-handedness
is not learnt as a child.

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:10.100
It’s not simply a matter of which hand a
child chooses to write with from an early

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:11.100
age.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:15.570
If this were true, the numbers would be closer
to 50/50 for left and right-handedness.

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:19.650
But only 10% of the population is left-handed.

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:24.070
In fact we can actually tell if a baby is
going to be left or right-handed when they’re

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:26.780
only a couple of months old.

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:31.220
When you place a baby on its tummy, babies’
who will grow up to be left-handed will typically

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:36.750
turn their heads to the left, whereas right-handers
do the opposite.

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:41.990
Before you go haphazardly flipping over babies
to try this out for yourself, you should know

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:46.810
it’s not an entirely accurate way to tell,
but research has shown there’s a strong

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:48.470
correlation.

00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:53.030
So if we don’t learn left-handedness, then
where does it come from?

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:56.610
Statistics suggest we’re born with it; it’s
in our genes.

00:01:56.610 --> 00:02:01.869
Two right-handed parents have a 9% chance
to give birth to a left-handed child.

00:02:01.869 --> 00:02:08.629
When one parent is left-handed that rises
to 19% and when both parents are left-handed

00:02:08.629 --> 00:02:11.230
the chance is 26%.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:15.040
These statistics suggest that handedness is
at least somewhat hereditary.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:21.310
But left handedness is highly unusual, because
it’s not simply caused by dominant and recessive

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:22.780
genes.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:28.670
About 90% of people are right-handed, suggesting
that right-handedness is an extremely dominant

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:29.800
trait.

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:34.620
Based on what we know about genetics, a gene
that is so fiercely dominant, in this case

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:41.470
right-handedness, would have forced the recessive
gene, left-handedness, out of the gene pool

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:43.489
a long time ago.

00:02:43.489 --> 00:02:46.580
In theory, we shouldn’t have left-handed
people.

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:52.239
Yet we still do and the percentage of people
that are born left-handed isn’t decreasing

00:02:52.239 --> 00:02:55.150
like it theoretically should do.

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:59.410
In fact, it has stayed exactly the same for
thousands of years.

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:04.320
This suggests that handedness isn’t caused
by a simple case of dominant vs recessive

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:05.320
genes.

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:07.250
It’s considerably more complex than that.

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:12.240
It’s likely to be caused by a whole mix
of different genes or perhaps something completely

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.250
different altogether.

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:20.069
The truth is that, why some people favour
one hand over the other is still a bit of

00:03:20.069 --> 00:03:21.069
a mystery.

00:03:21.069 --> 00:03:25.230
There is one theory however that is the most
commonly accepted answer to this perennial

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:26.480
question.

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:30.580
Researchers think handedness is actually caused
by something called “brain lateralisation”.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:36.000
Our brains are divided into two hemispheres,
left and right.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:40.360
For the sake of efficiency our brains like
to use different regions for different tasks.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:45.909
Two of the most energy intensive activities
that humans do are language and using our

00:03:45.909 --> 00:03:47.800
fine motor skills.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:52.260
So our brain clusters the control of these
activities into one side of our brain, rather

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:55.430
than having it spread out all over the damn
place.

00:03:55.430 --> 00:03:58.400
This makes those tasks more energy efficient.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:02.629
Most people’s language and fine motor skills
are controlled by the left hemisphere of their

00:04:02.629 --> 00:04:07.480
brain and each hemisphere generally controls
the opposite side of the body.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:12.250
So it makes sense that most people would be
right handed, because in most people, the

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:17.019
majority of the processing which controls
the movement of muscles is done in the left

00:04:17.019 --> 00:04:23.039
hemisphere of the brain, which is the hemisphere
that controls the right hand side of the body.

00:04:23.039 --> 00:04:28.271
In fact, in 90% of right-handed individuals,
they use the left hemisphere of their brain

00:04:28.271 --> 00:04:30.970
to control language and fine motor skills.

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:36.690
Whereas, a considerably lower 61% of left
handers control these skills using the left

00:04:36.690 --> 00:04:38.300
side of their brain.

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:43.460
In most animals the hemispheres of their brain
divide the processing of tasks equally, those

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:46.569
same animals have no hand preference.

00:04:46.569 --> 00:04:51.529
Whereas human brains tend to specialise functions
to either one side of the brain or the other

00:04:51.529 --> 00:04:56.129
and consequently we also favour a particular
hand.

00:04:56.129 --> 00:05:01.240
This strong correlation has led biologists
to think that brain lateralisation is closely

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:03.349
linked to handedness.

00:05:03.349 --> 00:05:08.129
Left-hemisphere brain lateralisation is a
common trend amongst left handers but it doesn’t

00:05:08.129 --> 00:05:11.849
fully explain why people are left handed.

00:05:11.849 --> 00:05:17.659
After all, 61% of left handers still use the
left hemisphere of their brain, the same side

00:05:17.659 --> 00:05:19.860
that right handers use.

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:24.419
Researchers at Pennsylvania State University
believe handedness it caused by genes.

00:05:24.419 --> 00:05:29.550
Their theory is that there are two distinct
alleles of a gene which causes handedness.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:32.580
An allele is a variation of a gene.

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:37.740
One of those alleles is known as the D gene,
which stands for “dextral”, meaning right.

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:41.539
The other allele is called the C gene, which
stands for chance.

00:05:41.539 --> 00:05:46.039
The D gene is the most common in the human
gene pool and when it is present, the person

00:05:46.039 --> 00:05:48.809
will be always be, right-handed.

00:05:48.809 --> 00:05:53.551
You may therefore think that the presence
of the significantly less common C gene, will

00:05:53.551 --> 00:05:55.770
mean the person is left-handed.

00:05:55.770 --> 00:06:00.030
But it’s known as the chance gene, because
when it’s present, the hand preference of

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:05.119
the person will be random, there will be a
50/50 chance of that person being left or

00:06:05.119 --> 00:06:06.580
right handed.

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:09.069
This means that there’s a third class of
handedness.

00:06:09.069 --> 00:06:14.580
There’s a small percentage of people who
have some degree of ambidexterity.

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:18.740
Being ambidextrous means one is equally as
proficient with both hands.

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:24.409
Since genes come in pairs, every human has
one of three combinations of the aforementioned

00:06:24.409 --> 00:06:26.610
D and C genes.

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:32.319
The first combination is DD, meaning the person
has a strong right-handed bias.

00:06:32.319 --> 00:06:37.649
The second combination is CC, meaning there’s
a straight up 50/50 chance the person will

00:06:37.649 --> 00:06:39.580
be either left or right-handed.

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:47.610
But the third combination is quite unusual;
the third possibility is DC, one of each gene

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:48.990
variation.

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:54.569
People with both a D (right-handed) and a
C (chance) gene, are usually most proficient

00:06:54.569 --> 00:07:00.659
with their right hand, but they are also perfectly
capable using their left hand.

00:07:00.659 --> 00:07:06.649
People who have a DC gene combination are
somewhere in the spectrum of being semi-ambidextrous

00:07:06.649 --> 00:07:09.139
to fully ambidextrous.

00:07:09.139 --> 00:07:12.400
Such people make up only 1% of the population.

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:18.279
So if you are one of the 1% that can adequately
use both hands, well done, you have a very

00:07:18.279 --> 00:07:20.050
rare set of genes.

00:07:20.050 --> 00:07:23.479
But if you are left-handed it’s not all
bad news.

00:07:23.479 --> 00:07:26.479
There’s numerous benefits to being a lefty.

00:07:26.479 --> 00:07:29.199
Lefties are sought after in competitive sports.

00:07:29.199 --> 00:07:34.409
Since most players are right-handed, a lefty
can surprise and unnerve their opponent, gaining

00:07:34.409 --> 00:07:35.810
the advantage.

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:41.119
Because most players are used to fighting
right-handed opponents, not left-handers.

00:07:41.119 --> 00:07:47.469
Sports where left handers have such an advantage
include tennis, baseball and boxing, to name

00:07:47.469 --> 00:07:48.770
but a few.

00:07:48.770 --> 00:07:53.629
Also, scientists aren’t quite sure why,
but lefties are considerably more likely to

00:07:53.629 --> 00:07:56.459
being a genius than righties.

00:07:56.459 --> 00:08:02.709
For example, 20% of Mensa members are left-handed,
which is a disproportionately large amount

00:08:02.709 --> 00:08:06.959
when you consider that only 10% of the population
are left-handed.

00:08:06.959 --> 00:08:10.289
Some believe lefties are more intelligent
because throughout their life, they’ve been

00:08:10.289 --> 00:08:16.360
forced to use and workout both sides of their
brains instead of just the one.

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:21.089
Also an unusually high percentage of US Presidents
have been left handed.

00:08:21.089 --> 00:08:23.889
Including Barack Obama, Bill Clinton, George
H.W.

00:08:23.889 --> 00:08:26.219
Bush and Ronald Reagan.

00:08:26.219 --> 00:08:31.490
There are endless benefits to being a lefty,
so even if the word “left” is synonymous

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:33.770
with being evil, don’t worry.

00:08:33.770 --> 00:08:38.469
Next time your friend teases you for being
a lefty, just remind them that you’re considerably

00:08:38.469 --> 00:08:43.409
more likely to be accepted into Mensa and
you stand a much better chance than they do

00:08:43.409 --> 00:09:10.230
at becoming president.

